# Claude Code Instructions

## MANDATORY: Pre-Session Reading

Before starting ANY work on this project, you MUST read the following files in order:

1. **`README.md`** — Project overview, features, installation, configuration, API reference, and the Agent & AI Workflow section
2. **`CHANGELOG.md`** — Full version history; understand what has changed and why before touching any code
3. **`chat/*.md`** — All previous AI development sessions (one file per session, named `subject-date.md`); contains decisions made, patterns established, and context that must not be lost

Failure to read these files before working risks duplicating effort, reversing past decisions, or breaking established patterns.

## MANDATORY: Post-Session Logging

After completing any work session, you MUST:

1. Create a new file in `chat/` named `subject-date.md` (e.g., `fix-login-error-2026-04-26.md`) following the existing per-session format
2. Update the `## [Unreleased]` section in `CHANGELOG.md` if any code changes were made
3. Keep entries concise but complete — include all files modified and decisions made

## Package Manager
- Always use `yarn` as the package manager for this project
- Never use `npm` for installing, updating, or managing dependencies
- When adding packages, use: `yarn add <package>`
- When removing packages, use: `yarn remove <package>`
- When installing dependencies, use: `yarn install`

## File Creation
- Never create unnecessary markdown (.md) files or documentation files
- Only create documentation files when explicitly requested by the user
- Prefer editing existing files over creating new ones

## API Calls
- Always use `call` function from `@/utils/apiWrapper` for API calls
- Never use `window.frappe.call` or `frappe.call` directly
- Import as: `import { call } from "@/utils/apiWrapper"`
